# 🐞 Same-project rehome loses canonical nested mapping and review dry-run collides with MCP content — scribe_rehome_resolution_fix_20260830
**Author:** Scribe
**Version:** v0.1
**Status:** INVESTIGATING
**Last Updated:** 2026-08-30 06:34:30 UTC

> Summarise why this document exists and what decisions it captures.

---
## Bug Overview
<!-- ID: bug_overview -->
**Symptoms:** A successful same-project review rehome moved the file into `contracts/`, but the next canonical-name write resolved the deleted project-root path. Special review create dry-runs also failed MCP host result validation because `content` was a string.

**Customer impact:** The governed create → rehome → populate workflow was unusable for nested review documents, forcing callers toward path-based writes that the safety boundary rejects. Dry-run callers could not safely preview special review creation through the host.


---
## Description
<!-- ID: description -->
### Summary
After rehoming REVIEW_CI_RUNNER_01 into a nested same-project contracts path, the next replace_section by canonical doc name resolves the removed root path. A special review create dry-run also returns top-level content as a string, causing host response validation to reject it.

### Expected Behaviour
The canonical doc name resolves the nested target immediately and after project rebind, with no stale source mapping. Dry-run create returns a non-mutating host-valid result whose MCP content envelope is a sequence.

### Actual Behaviour
After rehoming REVIEW_CI_RUNNER_01 into a nested same-project contracts path, the next replace_section by canonical doc name resolves the removed root path. A special review create dry-run also returns top-level content as a string, causing host response validation to reject it.

### Steps to Reproduce
- [ ] Create special review doc REVIEW_CI_RUNNER_01.
- [ ] Rehome it within the same project to contracts/REVIEW_CI_RUNNER_01.md using target_doc_name REVIEW_CI_RUNNER_01.
- [ ] Call replace_section by canonical doc name and observe auto-registration targeting the removed root file.
- [ ] Call special review create with dry_run=True through the MCP host and observe reserved content shape validation failure.



---
## Investigation
<!-- ID: investigation -->
**Root Cause Analysis:**
Same-project rehome computed and persisted separate source and target doc maps, then refreshed the active project with the source map whose canonical key was removed. Special-create dry-runs placed rendered markdown in top-level content, colliding with MCP CallToolResult.content sequence semantics.

**Affected Areas:**
- src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/runtime.py
- tests/test_manage_docs_cleanup_support.py
- tests/test_manage_docs_create_intent.py


**Related Issues:**
- Link to related bugs, tickets, or documentation.


---
## Resolution Plan
<!-- ID: resolution_plan -->
### Immediate Actions
- [ ] Use one canonical docs map for same-project moves, persist/refresh it once, and move string-valued dry-run content to preview after section inventory. Add hermetic regression tests for immediate write, durable rebind, absence of stale source mapping, host content shape, and no dry-run side effects.


### Long-Term Fixes
- [ ] Outline long-term remedial work or refactors.

### Testing Strategy
- [ ] Define validation steps for the fix (unit, integration, regression).


